WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
On the Home screen, click Open project… and choose the copy of the second tutorial’s project.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
The project opens up to date: nothing is to be computed.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Click Inspect: the final image of the workflow is shown.

4
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Choose 100 % in the zoom list.

5
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Drag the frame of the overview onto the star field to the right of the cluster.

6
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:25.000
At 100 %, the stars are a little soft: median width 4.84 px, 279 stars detected. The gas and the sky are right.

7
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Click Graph.

8
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Right-click the Gradient block.

9
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Click Variant here: a second workflow starts after Gradient.

10
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Calibration, registration and stacking are shared by the two workflows: they are not computed again.

11
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Double-click Deconvolution in the palette: the block is added to the variant, after Gradient.

12
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Choose Neural network (beta).

13
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Click Run: only the variant’s blocks are computed.

14
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:59.000
The list shows everything up to date except the variant’s Deconvolution, Denoise and Stars/background.

15
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:05.000
Not shown in real time: the run took 3 min 08 s.

16
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Click Inspect: the page opens on the variant’s Deconvolution block, before and after the block on each side of a divider.

17
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.000
Choose 100 % in the zoom list.

18
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.000
Drag the frame of the overview onto the same star field.

19
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:21.000
Drag the divider across the stars: before the block on its left, after on its right.

20
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:29.000
Stars: tighter, median width 4.84 to 4.19 px, and 37 % more faint stars detected. The gas and the faint arc are unchanged.

21
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Click Post: the two workflows give two layers.

22
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:37.000
The variant’s layer is the top one, its eye switched off: the original shows.

23
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Click the variant’s layer.

24
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:43.000
Drag Strength to −0.5, as on the original’s layer.

25
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.000
Drag Small stars to −1.0.

26
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.000
Drag Sky to −1.5.

27
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Drag Faint tones to +1.0.

28
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.000
Click the eye of the top layer: the variant covers the original.

29
00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:00.000
On the fitted view, the two pictures are almost the same.

30
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.000
Click the eye again: the original shows.

31
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.000
Zoom to about 100 % on the star field (Ctrl and the mouse wheel).

32
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:11.000
Click the eye: the variant’s stars are tighter.

33
00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:16.000
Click it again: the original’s stars.

34
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.000
Click Graph.

35
00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.000
Right-click a block of the variant.

36
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.000
Point at the Workflow entry of the menu.

37
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:31.000
Click Delete workflow: the variant goes, the original stays.

38
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:35.000
The project is saved with the original workflow only.
